architectural_invariants:
  - KOS-Lab authority preserved
  - KOS-Comm autonomy preserved
  - explicit Binding is the bilateral seam
  - KCA must remain neutral
  - KCP must remain small and replaceable
  - KSCL decomposition remains open until AR-5
  - receipt != canonical import
  - communication != authority
  - representation != represented object
  - representation != authority
  - reconstruction != authorization
  - promotion to KOS-Lab requires evidence + governance

closed_items:
  - Gate 0 architectural consensus
  - KOS-Lab <-> KOS-Comm reconciliation
  - AR-1 Boundary Model

active_work_item:
  id: AR-2
  name_es: Modelo de representación
  name_en: Representation Model
  state: ACTIVE_PAUSED_FOR_CONTINUITY_IMPLEMENTATION

active_hypotheses:
  - referent / representation / encoded form are distinct levels
  - representation identity != subject identity
  - semantic context must be explicit enough for interpretation
  - provenance and references require neutral semantics
  - completeness must be scoped
  - authority remains external to representation
  - non-KOS neutrality is mandatory
  - RepresentationEnvelope is conceptual and must not become a premature protocol message format

ar_2_validation_plan:
  - reference without object transfer
  - partial state observation
  - operational result
  - local projection
  - evidence associated with a claim
  - proposal without incorporation authority
  - derived representation with known loss
  - reconstructable representation
  - composite representation
  - non-KOS <-> non-KOS exchange
  - same representation with two encodings
  - two representations of the same subject

open_questions:
  - common mandatory structure vs semantic capability set
  - fundamental representation classes vs domain specializations
  - neutral subject identity
  - claim vs evidence vs verified guarantee
  - mandatory vs class-dependent provenance
  - neutral completeness/coverage semantics
  - representation relationships without mandatory universal graph
  - minimum metadata outside source system
  - prevention of RepresentationEnvelope becoming protocol framing

continuity_decisions:
  - KSCL is used experimentally for semantic continuity before AR-5
  - KSCL records do not have architectural authority
  - Git verification remains mandatory during reentry
  - CURRENT.kscl is mutable current state
  - checkpoint files are historical semantic snapshots

next_action:
  phase: AR-2
  action: first validation pass
  objective: validate 12 scenarios and refine taxonomy/capabilities
  decision_target: determine common structure vs semantic capability model

reentry_sequence:
  - read REENTRY-GUIDE
  - read REENTRY-CHECKPOINT
  - read CURRENT.kscl
  - verify repository, branch and actual HEAD
  - read AR-1 closure
  - read AR-2 active model
  - reconcile any later evidence
  - declare state and next action

assertions:
  - KSCL continuity != architectural authority
  - KSCL record != Git verification
  - KSCL reconstruction != proof
  - checkpoint state != actual Git state until verified
